{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>A night of watchings it is to YHWH.</b> According to the plain sense, because it mentions \"a night of watchings it is to YHWH,\" and at the end \"watchings for all the children of Israel for their generations\" — the meaning appears to be that because HaShem watched over them and did not allow the destroyer to enter their houses to strike, He commanded that this night be watchings for all the children of Israel for their generations. And the meaning is the eating of the Passover according to its ordinance, and unleavened bread and bitter herbs on this night. And there are some who interpret it like the sense of \"watchmen of the walls\" (Song of Songs 5:7) — that they did not sleep but rather gave thanks and recounted the might of HaShem at their going out from Egypt. And thus our sages of blessed memory hinted: \"The time has arrived for reciting Shema of the morning\" (Passover Haggadah)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:56.676869848Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}